# DNS change request (template) — ingress replication path

**Purpose:** Paste into a DNS-team change ticket before cutover when using a **dedicated ingress shard** on the replication VLAN (Path B in the [architecture overview](../../messaging/kafka/cross-dc-architecture-overview.md)).

**Source data:** Fill from inventory `ingress.*` fields or manually from `render-config.py` output context. See [inventory-dc-a.ingress.example.yaml](../inventory-dc-a.ingress.example.yaml).

---

## Summary

Publish internal DNS so remote datacenter brokers resolve **Kafka replication Route hostnames** to addresses on the **replication VLAN** — not the default `apps.*` ingress VIP.

## Zones (one per datacenter)

| DC | Zone | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| ${dc_a_id} | `${dc_a_ingress_domain}` | CFK Route hostnames for DC-A brokers |
| ${dc_b_id} | `${dc_b_ingress_domain}` | CFK Route hostnames for DC-B brokers |

## Required records

### Wildcard (recommended)

Covers all CFK-created broker and bootstrap hostnames (`repl-b1.${domain}`, etc.):

| Name | Type | Targets | TTL |
|---|---|---|---|
| `*.${dc_a_ingress_domain}` | A | ${dc_a_dns_targets} | ${dns_ttl} |
| `*.${dc_b_ingress_domain}` | A | ${dc_b_dns_targets} | ${dns_ttl} |

`${dc_a_dns_targets}` / `${dc_b_dns_targets}` — comma-separated list:

- **VIP mode:** single replication-subnet VIP per DC (e.g. `10.200.1.5`)
- **DNS LB mode:** repl NIC IPs of nodes running the replication IngressController (e.g. `10.200.1.11`, `10.200.1.12`, `10.200.1.13`)

### Cross-DC resolution

Resolvers in **each** datacenter must be able to query the **other** DC's zone (conditional forwarder or shared internal DNS).

## Explicit non-goals

- Do **not** point replication hostnames at the machine-network `apps.*` ingress VIP.
- Do **not** publish these names on public DNS unless the replication path is genuinely internet-routed (unusual).

## TLS note (passthrough)

Router does not terminate TLS; broker certs must include SANs matching the Route hostnames. No wildcard cert required **on the router**.

## Verification

From the remote DC: `dig repl-b1.${dc_a_ingress_domain}` returns a replication-subnet IP, not the management ingress VIP.

Platform reference: [cross-dc-ingress-alternative.md — external dependencies](../../messaging/kafka/cross-dc-ingress-alternative.md#external-dependencies-handoff).
